{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Rebecca said.</b> The addition of the vav indicates that she concurred with the holy spirit that rested upon her." "<b>saying, Behold, etc.</b> Meaning: lest he think that a long time had already passed since Yitzhak spoke to Esav, and he say that he would not be able to fulfill Rebecca's instruction in time before Esav had already done his deed — therefore she said <b>saying, Behold</b>, meaning she told him that she heard at that very moment, and there is still time." "<b>your brother, saying.</b> Meaning: not your brother in resemblance to you, but in speech he would call him by the name ״your brother,״ yet darkness does not resemble the light of the world." "<b>Further,</b> she intended in her saying <b>saying</b>, not to let a falsehood proceed from her mouth, for she did not say the words with the exactness of how they came forth from Yitzhak's mouth. Therefore she said ״saying, bring״ etc. — meaning: what he intended in his saying is this; and without ״saying״ it would have been heard as though she were reciting his words with exactness."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:46.177910434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}